# Prerequisites
*.d

# Object files
*.o
*.ko
*.obj
*.elf

# Linker output
*.ilk
*.map
*.exp
*.sys
*.sym
*.err
*.log
# The DDK's build.exe appends BUILD_ALT_DIR to TARGETPATH, so `obj` in
# src\sources becomes objfre (release), objchk (debug) or objchk_qemu (the
# qemu flavour, task 13-L.1) - none of which matches obj/. The third name is
# what keeps the two *checked* builds from overwriting each other's objects;
# see scripts\build-driver.cmd :buildflavor.
obj/
objchk/
objchk_qemu/
objfre/

# Precompiled Headers
*.gch
*.pch

# Libraries
*.lib
*.a
*.la
*.lo

# Shared objects (inc. Windows DLLs)
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib

# Executables
*.exe
*.out
*.app
*.i*86
*.x86_64
*.hex

# Debug files
*.dSYM/
*.su
*.idb
*.pdb

# Kernel Module Compile Results
*.mod*
*.cmd
# ...but this project's build/test scripts are .cmd files. Without these
# negations they are silently ignored (the tracked ones had to be git add -f).
!xhciqual/build.cmd
!xhcisnap/build.cmd
!xhciqual/test/*.cmd
!scripts/**/*.cmd
!test/*.cmd
.tmp_versions/
modules.order
Module.symvers
Mkfile.old
dkms.conf

# debug information files
*.dwo

# Local toolchain archives (keep only the boot-image URL template tracked)
tools/*
!tools/w98se.url.example

# Phase 1 local VM/setup outputs
vm/
scripts/local/

# Staged install media (scripts\package\make-package.ps1). Generated from the
# built driver, the tracked INF, and the git-ignored per-target usbd.sys
# sources under tools\ - reproducible, and half of it not ours.
#
# make-release.ps1 also assembles the GitHub release asset here as
# out\upload-<version>\ and .zip. That tree deliberately contains every
# Microsoft file scripts\package\usbd-sources.expected names - the two usbd.sys
# builds and usbhub98.sys since batch 13-E - so it must stay ignored: publishing
# them as a
# release asset is a decision (docs\contributing\legal-provenance.md section 5),
# committing them is not, and a git blob cannot be withdrawn the way an asset
# can.
out/

# Published releases (scripts\package\make-release.ps1) ARE tracked, binaries
# included - that is the whole difference between releases\ and out\ above. The
# global *.sys rule near the top would otherwise swallow them silently, so undo
# it for this directory only. Only the two files this project owns can ever land
# here: usbd98.sys, usbd2k.sys and usbhub98.sys are Microsoft's and are excluded
# by the script, not by this rule - see releases\README.md.
#
# The *.exe and *.map pair is the DOS qualifier staged into each release. Its
# MAP is what turns a fault address on a photographed DOS screen back into a
# source location, and it only matches the EXE built with it - which is exactly
# the argument the qualification-run rule below already makes for evidence, so
# the two travel together here too.
!releases/**/*.sys
!releases/**/*.exe
!releases/**/*.map

# make-release.ps1's two working directories, which exist only while a release
# is being cut: `.staging-<version>` is the tree under construction, and
# `.replaced-<version>` is the previous release held aside so a failed publish
# can put it back. A run that is interrupted between the two renames leaves one
# behind, and the danger is specific - `.replaced-*` holds a COMPLETE former
# release, binaries included, so without these rules the un-negated `*.sys` line
# above would not save it and a `git add -A` would commit a second, differently
# named copy of a published version.
#
# The script treats the two differently, and deliberately: a leftover
# `.staging-*` is scratch and is cleared, while a leftover `.replaced-*` makes
# it REFUSE to run - that one may be the only copy of a published version on
# the machine, so which copy is authoritative is not a script's decision.
releases/.staging-*/
releases/.replaced-*/

# Per-run scratch from scripts\package\test-package.ps1. It has to live inside
# the repository because manifest SOURCE paths are repo-relative and may not
# escape it, and it is GUID-named so concurrent runs cannot share state. The
# test removes only what it created, so a normal or failing run leaves nothing
# behind - but an interrupted one would otherwise leave the tree looking dirty.
scripts/package/.testsrc-*/

# Local mirror of upstream reference sources (keep only its README tracked)
external/*
!external/README.md

# Third-party specification documents. Each is fetched by whoever needs it from
# the official URL recorded in docs/references/README.md, which also carries the
# version and SHA-256 to check the download against. They are not this
# project's to redistribute: the Intel xHCI specification reserves all rights
# and grants no licence in the document itself, and the USB-IF backwards-
# compatibility test document is licensed "FOR INTERNAL USE ONLY". Ignore the
# whole directory rather than a *.pdf pattern - AGENTS.md sends every
# third-party document here, and the next one may not be a PDF. Keep only the
# README tracked - see docs/contributing/legal-provenance.md.
docs/references/*
!docs/references/README.md

# Phase 0 qualification tool: build outputs fall under the global
# patterns above; keep its scripts tracked despite *.cmd
!xhciqual/build.cmd
!xhciqual/test/run-qemu-test.cmd
xhciqual/test/hdd/
xhciqual/test/win98hdd/
xhciqual/test/usb.img
xhciqual/*.lst

# xhcisnap's own dumps: raw extension images and PORTSC arrays taken off a
# target. Evidence, not source - they belong in vm/ or an attached report.
xhcisnap/*.BIN
xhcisnap/*.PSC
xhcisnap/*.bin
xhcisnap/*.psc
xhciqual/test/*.bin
xhciqual/test/*.ppm

# temp/ is scratch, and only scratch. The operator's bench dumps land there by
# hand, one set per boot, and are copied off to a tracked evidence directory if
# a document ends up citing them - `docs/contributing/runs/run-13e-evidence/` is
# the 13-E sessions'. Nothing in temp/ is tracked; a dump still sitting here is
# one no document depends on.
#
# Ignore the *contents* rather than the directory, for the reason spelled out at
# `.claude/*` below: git does not descend into an ignored directory, so a
# negation could not be added afterwards. That is not hypothetical here - seven
# dumps were tracked in temp/ until batch 13-R precisely because documents cited
# them.
temp/*

# Archived bare-metal qualification runs are evidence, not build output:
# keep them despite the global *.log rule (case-insensitive on Windows).
# The linker MAP archived beside them is what turns a photographed DOS/32A
# fault EIP back into a symbol, so it is evidence too - keep it despite *.map.
!xhciqual/results/**/*.LOG
!xhciqual/results/**/*.MAP

# macOS / OneDrive cruft
.DS_Store

# Repo-local Claude state and working notes are not part of the codebase
# (`memory/` moved here from ~/.claude/projects/.../memory; see
# CLAUDE.md). Ignore the contents rather than the directory itself: git does
# not descend into an ignored directory, so `.claude/` would make the
# settings.json negation below impossible to add later.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json

# Phase 10: the per-host device-matrix config (copy of config.sample.psd1 beside
# it). Lives with the harness, not at the repo root; the loaders look only here.
scripts/vm-matrix/matrix.config.psd1
